  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-11-02 on dev ae02786fca (WI-jomik acceptance sweep, after PR #2004: shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates; PR #2006: a Rust method call never binds a free function). VERDICT: STILL_REPRODUCES. Repro run: Residual 1 is the description’s own fixture /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/kizih/app.py (import socket; def g(): import mysock as socket; def f(h): s = socket.socket(h); s.send(b’x’)); control /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/kizih_ctl has no g(). Residual 3 is /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/kizih3/app.py (import os; def lam(): return (lambd. Observed: Residual 1: calls python:app.py:4-5:f:function -> python:mysock:0-0:socket:external_symbol L5. Control without g: f -> python:socket:0-0:socket and python:socket.socket:0-0:send (type_inferred). Residual 3: module_attr_ref python:app.py:4-5:lam:function -> python:os:0-0:os.environ:external_symbol L5 conf=0.85.. Note: Residual 3 needs a module-level `import os`. A lone `(lambda os: os.environ)(1)` with no import emits nothing. Residuals 2, 4 and 5 were not re-checked. Fixtures: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_*/."  # f4af
